=================================================
MODULE TYPES
=================================================

Standard Module
-------------------------------------------------

Uses standard ROPE workflows.

Examples:

- Tetraloop (T)
- KissingLoop (K)
- Bulge

Properties:

- Sequence matching
- Standard build logic
- Standard validation


Segmented Module
-------------------------------------------------

Separate module class.

Examples:

- Pepper
- Mango
- Broccoli
- Cilivia

Properties:

- Segmented matching
- Segmented build logic
- Segmented validation


Nonstandard Module
-------------------------------------------------

Last resort category.

Definition:

A module that breaks at least one standard ROPE
workflow and therefore requires special handling.

Examples:

- H1 (Base)
- H2 (Helix)
- X (Crossover)

Properties:

- Special mapper/build/validation logic
- Must be manually validated
- Must include a justification


=================================================
NONSTANDARD RULES
=================================================

If:

    nonstandard = true

then:

    reason = "..."

is required.

Nonstandard should NOT be the easy solution.

It means:

    "I cannot currently model this cleanly using
    the standard ROPE architecture."

Examples:

H1
-------------------------------------------------

reason =
"Fallback module assigned to unmapped residues.
Breaks standard mapping and validation."

H2
-------------------------------------------------

reason =
"Uses pair-based assignment and custom build
logic. Breaks standard validation."

X
-------------------------------------------------

reason =
"Topology module using ^ sequence markers.
Requires custom build logic and breaks standard
validation."


=================================================
MODULE.TOML FORMAT
=================================================

Standard Module
-------------------------------------------------

[metadata]
name = "Tetraloop"
source = "ROAD"

[module]
symbol = "T"
type = "module"
priority = 2
sequence = "NUUCGN"

[default]
file = "Tetraloop.pdb"


Nonstandard Module
-------------------------------------------------

[metadata]
name = "Crossover"
source = "ROAD"

[module]
symbol = "X"
type = "module"
priority = 0

sequence = "NNN^NNNN"

nonstandard = true
reason = "Topology module using ^ sequence markers.
Requires custom build logic and breaks standard
validation."

[default]
file = "crossover.pdb"


Segmented Module
-------------------------------------------------

[metadata]
name = "Pepper"

[module]
symbol = "P"
type = "segmented"
priority = 2

sequence = [
    "NNNACUGGCGCCNNN",
    "NNNCAAUCGUGGCGUGUCGNNN"
]

spacer = [
    "CCUUCGGG"
]

[default]
file = "Pepper_6HBC.pdb"

[[variants]]
name = "HBC620"
file = "7eop.pdb.gz"

[[variants]]
name = "HBC485"
file = "7eok.pdb.gz"


=================================================
LIBRARY INDEX
=================================================

library_index

Purpose:

- Official validated module registry.
- Maintained by ROPE developers.
- Committed to git.

Generated by:

    rope-library --validate --rebuild

Example:

P|fluorescent/pepper|segmented
K|structural/kissingloop|module
X|structural/crossover|module

Source of Truth:

    module.toml

Library Manifest:

    library_index


