=================================================
MASTER_LIBRARY
=================================================

Contains all required modules and variants for the
current run.

Example:

MASTER_LIBRARY["P"] = {
    "default": Pepper_default,
    "HBC485": Pepper_HBC485,
    "HBC620": Pepper_HBC620
}

MASTER_LIBRARY["K"] = {
    "default": KissingLoop
}


=================================================
ACTIVE_LIBRARY
=================================================

One module per symbol.

Example:

ACTIVE_LIBRARY = {

    "H1": Base,

    "H2": Helix,

    "K": KissingLoop,

    "P": Pepper_HBC620
}

RNAbuild() only sees ACTIVE_LIBRARY.

Build code never handles variants directly.


=================================================
VARIANT HANDLING
=================================================

Current
-------------------------------------------------

set_variant()
reset()
_copy_state()

Problems:

- Mutable state
- Reset logic required
- Easy to misuse


Future
-------------------------------------------------

MASTER_LIBRARY["P"]["HBC620"]

↓

ACTIVE_LIBRARY["P"]

No mutation.

No reset.

No variant switching.


Deletion Targets
-------------------------------------------------

set_variant()

reset()

reset_variant()

_copy_state()

default_variant()


