=================================================
VALIDATION LEVELS
=================================================

TOML Validation
-------------------------------------------------

- Syntax valid
- Required fields present
- Types correct
- nonstandard requires reason


Package Validation
-------------------------------------------------

- Default file exists
- Variant files exist
- Blueprint files exist


Build Validation
-------------------------------------------------

- Module loads
- Validation build succeeds
- Output PDB generated


Structure Validation
-------------------------------------------------

- Sequence check
- Residue count
- Atom count
- Closure validation
- Segment validation


Nonstandard Modules
-------------------------------------------------

- Manual validation required
- Standard validation may be skipped


=================================================
FUTURE ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLE
=================================================

Create a new module class only when a reusable
concept emerges.

Examples:

Current:

- module
- segmented

Possible future:

- topological

Do NOT create new classes for one-off modules.

Use:

    nonstandard = true

for exceptional cases.

If multiple modules share the same special
behavior, promote that behavior into a proper
module class.


